  "content": {
    "id": "p97-q17-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Four campers have enough food for 20 weeks. How long will the food last if it is shared by 10 campers?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "8 weeks",
      "worked": "Let $t$ be the time in weeks and $c$ the number of campers. With a fixed food supply and equal consumption rates, time varies inversely with the number of campers.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}t&=\\frac{k}{c}\\\\20&=\\frac{k}{4}\\\\k&=80\\\\t&=\\frac{80}{10}\\\\t&=8\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe food will last 8 weeks.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 46
  },
